# Angular SPA Architecture Rules

You are building a production Angular SPA.

Follow these rules:

## Architecture

- Use standalone Angular components.
- Avoid NgModules unless required.
- Use feature-based folder structure.

Structure:

src/
 ├── app/
 │   ├── core/
 │   │   ├── services/
 │   │   ├── guards/
 │   │   └── interceptors/
 │   │
 │   ├── shared/
 │   │   ├── ui/
 │   │   ├── components/
 │   │   └── directives/
 │   │
 │   └── features/
 │       └── feature-name/
 │           ├── pages/
 │           ├── components/
 │           ├── services/
 │           └── models/


## Angular Style

Use:

- Signals instead of BehaviorSubject for local state.
- inject() instead of constructor injection.
- Typed reactive forms.
- Lazy loading routes.
- OnPush change detection.

Prefer:

signal()
computed()
effect()

Avoid:

any
large components
business logic inside templates


## Components

Every component must:

- have one responsibility
- have separated html/scss/ts files
- use semantic HTML
- support mobile layout
